{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019nBazYPi47sQJfASoy6N1n","type":"tool_result","content":"commit 8f9d5dcddb0094f42e6519630a35864582f8ddbf\nAuthor: Patrick Devaney <patrickbdevaney@gmail.com>\nDate:   Wed Aug 19 21:59:15 2026 -0400\n\n    0.2 measured: the context term is gone, and it retires two ladder items\n    \n    Two single-prompt DPROF runs on the same binary, ctx 480 and ctx 3000:\n    \n                  base AR      spec              i:topk(21)  i:score  cattn:indexer\n      ctx  480    89.3 ms/tok  65.9 = 15.18 t/s    0.10 ms   0.02 ms     2.09 ms\n      ctx 3000    89.4 ms/tok  65.2 = 15.33 t/s    0.10 ms   0.02 ms     2.05 ms\n    \n    Base AR moved 0.1 ms across a 6x context change. The pre-fix fit predicted 150.9 -> 226.6\n    over the same span. The context slope went from 30.05 ms per 1000 tokens to about 0.04,\n    and i:topk is flat at 0.10 ms across all 21 calls. Both LOSSLESS gates passed.\n    \n    This RETIRES ladder items 1.2 and 1.5 as performance levers. A single-CTA radix select\n    would replace a kernel that now costs 0.10 ms, and the index_score GEMM would attack a\n    0.02 ms mark; neither earns the bit-exactness risk that the research ranked them for. They\n    were ranked #1 and #3 on the strength of a cost model fitted BEFORE the warp fix, which is\n    exactly why the ladder requires a measurement between items rather than a plan executed\n    straight through. 1.3 and 1.4 stay, as correctness items.\n    \n    What remains is ATTENTION at 44 percent and MoE at 38 percent -- Term A, the term with\n    about 1.5x of headroom rather than 3x.\n    \n    Also adds dprobe after every launch in compressed_decode_step_indexer_dp. dprobe is gated\n    on DSV4_SYNCPROBE and compiles to one predicted branch otherwise, so this is free in normal\n    operation and turns the indexer decode path into a fully attributed walk when needed.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n DECODE_LADDER.md             | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++------\n kernels/compressed_decode.cu | 16 ++++++++--------\n 2 files changed, 35 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)\n----\ndprof5.log\ndprof6.log\ndprof_blk6_current.log\nprefill_dprof_b9b.log\nprefill_dprof_b9c.log\nprefill_dprof_b9d.log\nprefill_dprof_b9.log\nsrv_dprof.log","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa0d1aaa-07ff-4130-9262-391acc334eb4","uuid":"54474d80-9b80-4161-a4a5-00c6a865deaf","timestamp":"2026-08-20T03:05:26.693Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"commit 8f9d5dcddb0094f42e6519630a35864582f8ddbf\nAuthor: Patrick Devaney <patrickbdevaney@gmail.com>\nDate:   Wed Aug 19 21:59:15 2026 -0400\n\n    0.2 measured: the context term is gone, and it retires two ladder items\n    \n    Two single-prompt DPROF runs on the same binary, ctx 480 and ctx 3000:\n    \n                  base AR      spec              i:topk(21)  i:score  cattn:indexer\n      ctx  480    89.3 ms/tok  65.9 = 15.18 t/s    0.10 ms   0.02 ms     2.09 ms\n      ctx 3000    89.4 ms/tok  65.2 = 15.33 t/s    0.10 ms   0.02 ms     2.05 ms\n    \n    Base AR moved 0.1 ms across a 6x context change. The pre-fix fit predicted 150.9 -> 226.6\n    over the same span. The context slope went from 30.05 ms per 1000 tokens to about 0.04,\n    and i:topk is flat at 0.10 ms across all 21 calls. Both LOSSLESS gates passed.\n    \n    This RETIRES ladder items 1.2 and 1.5 as performance levers. A single-CTA radix select\n    would replace a kernel that now costs 0.10 ms, and the index_score GEMM would attack a\n    0.02 ms mark; neither earns the bit-exactness risk that the research ranked them for. They\n    were ranked #1 and #3 on the strength of a cost model fitted BEFORE the warp fix, which is\n    exactly why the ladder requires a measurement between items rather than a plan executed\n    straight through. 1.3 and 1.4 stay, as correctness items.\n    \n    What remains is ATTENTION at 44 percent and MoE at 38 percent -- Term A, the term with\n    about 1.5x of headroom rather than 3x.\n    \n    Also adds dprobe after every launch in compressed_decode_step_indexer_dp. dprobe is gated\n    on DSV4_SYNCPROBE and compiles to one predicted branch otherwise, so this is free in normal\n    operation and turns the indexer decode path into a fully attributed walk when needed.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n DECODE_LADDER.md             | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++------\n kernels/compressed_decode.cu | 16 ++++++++--------\n 2 files changed, 35 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)\n----\ndprof5.log\ndprof6.log\ndprof_blk6_current.log\nprefill_dprof_b9b.log\nprefill_dprof_b9c.log\nprefill_dprof_b9d.log\nprefill_dprof_b9.log\nsrv_dprof.log","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
